        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Send the global grid to the <computeroutput>diag_manager_mod</computeroutput> for regional output. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>In order for the diag_manager to do regional output for grids other than the standard lat/lon grid, the <computeroutput> diag_manager_mod</computeroutput> needs to know the latitude and longitude values for the entire global grid. This procedure is the mechanism the models will use to share their grid with the diagnostic manager.</para><para>This procedure needs to be called after the grid is created, and before the first call to register the fields.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">domain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The domain to which the grid data corresponds.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">glo_lat</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The latitude information for the grid tile.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">glo_lon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The longitude information for the grid tile.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">aglo_lat</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The latitude information for the a-grid tile.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">aglo_lon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The longitude information for the a-grid tile. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
